------------------------------------------------------------------------------
phase A: is C12 live? the cross-thread control (slots 28/29)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  thread 1 runs STALLWAIT(STALL_THREAD, CFGEXU)+NOP in slot 28 and NOP+NOP
  in slot 29; threads 0 and 2 run RMWCIB0+NOP in BOTH, so at t2/t3 they
  hold the Configuration Unit from outside thread 1's issue path. C12 is
  "Any thread has an instruction in any stage of the Configuration Unit
  pipeline", so a live C12 must make thread 1's stall grow with the
  number of hammering threads. Slot 29 carries the cross-thread issue
  interference that grows anyway, and subtracts it.

  variant thr    stall/pair    null/pair d = difference
  t1      1           2.968        1.996       +0.972
  t3      1           4.916        1.997       +2.919

TTBENCH_C12_LIVE: 0.9718 2.9186 t3
  d(t1) = 0.972 is the stall's own floor with nobody else in the unit.
  d(t3) = 2.919 is the same stall while two hammering thread(s) keep the
  unit busy. A large positive difference says C12 IS live, and then
  slots 22-25 reading zero means RDCFG's post-issue residency is no
  wider than the stall's own documented one-cycle lag. A zero says C12
  is inert on this part, and then slots 22-25 say nothing about RDCFG
  at all. Both are reachable; neither is the default.

